.TH TRIZBORT\-QT 1 "2026" "trizbort\-qt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trizbort\-qt \- map maker for interactive fiction and text adventures
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trizbort\-qt
.RI [ map.trizbort ]
.br
.B trizbort\-qt
.I map.trizbort
.B \-\-save
.I out.trizbort
.br
.B trizbort\-qt
.I map.trizbort
.BR \-\-zil | \-\-inform6 | \-\-inform7 | \-\-tads | \-\-hugo | \-\-alan | \-\-quest | \-\-adventuron
.I out
.br
.B trizbort\-qt
.I map.trizbort
.BR \-\-render " " \fIout.png\fR " | " \-\-pdf " " \fIout.pdf\fR " | " \-\-stats
.br
.B trizbort\-qt \-\-import\-transcript
.I play.txt out.trizbort
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trizbort\-qt
is a cross\-platform reimplementation of Trizbort, a mapper for interactive
fiction. It edits the \fB.trizbort\fR map format: rooms, the connections between
them, regions, colours and per\-map settings. With no arguments, or with a map
file, it opens the graphical editor. The command\-line options below run a task
without opening a window and then exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-save " file"
Load the map and write it back out (round\-trip / format upgrade).
.TP
.BI \-\-quicksave ", " \-q
Re\-save the map in place to its own file.
.TP
.BI \-\-smartsave ", " \-s
Re\-save the map and write a PDF and/or image beside it, per the Smart Save
preferences.
.TP
.BR \-\-zil ", " \-\-inform6 ", " \-\-inform7 ", " \-\-tads ", " \-\-hugo ", " \-\-alan ", " \-\-quest ", " \-\-questrooms ", " \-\-adventuron " " \fIfile\fR
Export the map as source code for the named interactive\-fiction system.
.TP
.BI \-\-render " file"
Render the map to a raster image (PNG, JPEG or BMP, by extension).
.TP
.BI \-\-pdf " file"
Render the map to a PDF document.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Print map statistics to standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-import\-transcript " in out"
Build a map from a play\-session transcript and write it to \fIout\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-loadlastproject ", " \-a
Open the most recently used map on start\-up.
.TP
.BR \-\-exit ", " \-x
After any batch task, do not open the editor window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/Trizbort/Trizbort (Qt).conf
Per\-user preferences (recent files, tooltips, export options).
.SH SEE ALSO
Project home page:
.UR https://www.trizbort.com/
.UE
.SH AUTHOR
Qt/C++ port by Jason Self. Based on the original C# Trizbort by Genstein and
Jason Lautzenheiser.
